<body>
    <h1>Api Design/Practice</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>discuss and confirm API doc before development</p></li>
</ol>
<p></p>
<p>2. API update, update related parties for the changes</p>
<p>use Google doc/ confluence page for better update and communication</p>
<p>swagger mark WHO using the api, when update, need to notify related part=
ies</p>
<p></p>
<h3 id=3D"ApiDesign/Practice-CommonPractice">Common Practice</h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>pagination</p></li>
</ol>
<p>1.1 index starts from <code>0</code></p>
<p>1.2 should return with <code>totalPages</code> to indicate the end</p>
<p>1.3 should return with <code>totalElements</code></p>
<p></p>
<p>From Chatgpt:</p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>While it is possible for the backend to return only the total number of =
elements and not the total number of pages in a paginated response, it is g=
enerally better to provide both.</p>
<p>Returning only the total number of elements can make it more difficult f=
or the API consumer to create a user interface that allows users to navigat=
e through the pages of results. They would need to know the page size or se=
t it themselves, and then calculate the number of pages based on the total =
number of elements.</p>
<p>On the other hand, providing both the total number of elements and the t=
otal number of pages makes it easier for the API consumer to build a user i=
nterface that displays the data correctly and enables users to navigate thr=
ough the pages of results.</p>
<p>Furthermore, returning the total number of pages can help the API consum=
er optimize their queries and reduce the number of API requests they need t=
o make. They can set their page size to a suitable number of items per page=
 and make a request for only the specific page they need.</p>
<p>Overall, providing both the total number of elements and the total numbe=
r of pages in a paginated response can make it easier for the API consumer =
to handle the response and create a user-friendly interface for users to na=
vigate through the results.</p>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"ApiDesign/Practice-errorcodeformatshouldsyncupbetweensystems">err=
or code format should sync up between systems</h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>API when not success response, must have the below error response</p></l=
i>
<li>
<p>define error response structure</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">{
  "error": {
    "code": "USER_NOT_FOUND",
    "message": "The requested user was not found."
  },
  "request": {
    "id": "abc123",
    "path": "/api/users/123",
    "timestamp": "2022-05-01T12:30:00.000Z"
  }
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<ul>
<li>
<p><code>error</code>: An object containing information about the error tha=
t occurred, including an error code and a human-readable error message.</p>=
</li>
<li>
<p><code>request</code>: An object containing information about the request=
 that triggered the error, including a unique request ID, the URL path of t=
he request, and a timestamp indicating when the request was made.</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p></p>
